---
/**
 * Disclaimer, the full, sitewide safety text. Compact variants of the same
 * wording ship with the Disclaimer component on module pages.
 */
import ArticleLayout from '../shared/layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../shared/components/Disclaimer.astro';
import { websiteJsonLd } from '../shared/seo/jsonld';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Satvik.fyi shares traditional wellness knowledge for education, it is not medical, psychological or spiritual advice. Read the full disclaimer."
  path="/disclaimer/"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  jsonLd={[websiteJsonLd(SITE)]}
>
  <p>
    Satvik.fyi exists to share the wisdom of the Indian traditions, ayurveda, yoga, pranayama,
    mantra and philosophy, in a careful, well-sourced way. Everything here is
    <strong>educational information about traditional systems</strong>, presented with their
    sources. It is not, and must not be used as, a substitute for professional advice.
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose my-8 space-y-4">
    <Disclaimer variant="general" />
    <Disclaimer variant="ayurveda" />
    <Disclaimer variant="yoga" />
    <Disclaimer variant="pranayama" />
  </div>

  <h2>Advanced practices</h2>
  <p>
    Some practices the traditions themselves gatekeep, advanced pranayama (kumbhaka and related
    breath retention), certain tantric material, and extended meditation retreats. Where this site
    describes them, it does so descriptively with content warnings, and points to learning them
    under qualified teachers rather than attempting them from a web page.
  </p>

  <h2>Sources and interpretation</h2>
  <p>
    Citations mark what a tradition actually says, in contrast with modern interpretation. Errors of
    translation or attribution can still occur; if you spot one, please
    <a href="/contact/">write in</a> and it will be corrected on the page.
  </p>

  <h2>No relationship</h2>
  <p>
    Use of this site does not create any practitioner–client, doctor–patient or teacher–student
    relationship with anyone involved in building it. If any content here conflicts with guidance
    from your own qualified practitioner or physician, follow your practitioner.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
